WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.060
Here's how to turn a phone, or anything with a web browser,

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.050
into a controller for PadForge.

3
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.330
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:12.900
On the Dashboard, tick Enable Web Controller Server.

5
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.260
The card then shows an address, and a QR code.

6
00:00:18.695 --> 00:00:20.795
Scan the code with your phone's camera,

7
00:00:20.835 --> 00:00:24.225
or open the address in any browser on the same network.

8
00:00:24.915 --> 00:00:26.765
Here, it's a browser on this PC.

9
00:00:29.273 --> 00:00:33.803
PadForge signs its own certificate, so the first visit shows a warning.

10
00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.063
Click Advanced, then Continue.

11
00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:38.163
The browser remembers the choice.

12
00:00:39.445 --> 00:00:40.495
Pick a layout.

13
00:00:40.865 --> 00:00:42.955
This is the Xbox 360 one.

14
00:00:43.405 --> 00:00:45.955
The page reloads once, and the controller appears.

15
00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:53.194
In PadForge, the Devices page lists the browser as an Xbox 360 web controller.

16
00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:56.354
Click it, and assign it to the virtual controller.

17
00:00:57.941 --> 00:01:00.051
Now drag the stick in the browser.

18
00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:04.211
Its axes move in PadForge, as a real controller's would.

19
00:01:05.491 --> 00:01:08.081
On a phone, the layout needs landscape.

20
00:01:08.631 --> 00:01:11.261
Add the page to your home screen to hide the address bar.

21
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:16.077
Find more guides at padforge.org.
